## Target Definitions (Surface 1)

Surface 1 prediction targets include:

### Binary Targets

* ES band downgrade within X days
* ES band upgrade within X days
* Crisis pattern trigger within X days
* Urgency escalation to Immediate within X days
* EVI enters High/Extreme tier within X days

### Multiclass Targets

* Next ES Band state (ES1–ES5)
* Next Pattern classification
* Next Urgency band

### Regression Targets

* ERI delta next window
* EVI delta next window

### Time-to-Event Targets

* Days until ES4 (Active Crisis)
* Days until ES5 (Critical Failure)
* Days until P0 priority

Time horizons must be explicit (e.g., 14 / 30 / 60 / 90 days).

---

## Model Characteristics

Surface 1 models operate as:

* State-transition classifiers
* Hazard models for escalation
* Tier-crossing probability estimators
* Structured temporal regression models

They predict forward structural migration, not raw emotional averages.

---

## Purpose

Surface 1 enables:

* Early warning before crisis classification
* Preemptive intervention routing
* Stabilization forecasting
* Structural risk identification
* Prioritization before degradation becomes visible

